#### RAF loop body — `private readonly _tick = (): void`

This is the hot path. Zero object allocation. All math operates on primitive numbers and pre-allocated fields.

```
_tick():
  if disposed or not rendering → return
  rafId = requestAnimationFrame(_tick)
  delta = min(clock.getDelta(), 0.1)   // MAX_DELTA_SECONDS

  // 1. Dampen velocity
  _scrollVelocity *= SCROLL_DAMPING^(delta * 60)   // frame-rate independent
  if abs(_scrollVelocity) < 0.0001 → _scrollVelocity = 0

  // 2. Update each plane
  for each record in _planes:
    data = record.data
    // advance z
    data.z += _scrollVelocity * delta * 10
    // wrap at [0, DEPTH_RANGE)
    if data.z >= DEPTH_RANGE:
      data.z -= DEPTH_RANGE
      data.imageIndex = (data.imageIndex + 1) % textureCount
      // swap texture on the material — the ONE allowed per-plane texture swap
      // (triggered only on wrap, not every frame)
      record.mesh.material.uniforms.map.value = _textures[data.imageIndex]
      record.mesh.material.needsUpdate = true
    else if data.z < 0:
      data.z += DEPTH_RANGE
      data.imageIndex = (data.imageIndex - 1 + textureCount) % textureCount
      record.mesh.material.uniforms.map.value = _textures[data.imageIndex]
      record.mesh.material.needsUpdate = true
    // update world Z
    worldZ = data.z - HALF_RANGE
    record.mesh.position.z = worldZ

    // normalised position
    n = data.z / DEPTH_RANGE

    // opacity
    opacity = computed via piecewise lerp using FADE_IN_*/FADE_OUT_* thresholds
    record.mesh.material.uniforms.opacity.value = opacity

    // blur
    blur = computed via piecewise lerp using BLUR_IN_*/BLUR_OUT_* thresholds
    record.mesh.material.uniforms.blurAmount.value = blur

    // scrollForce
    record.mesh.material.uniforms.scrollForce.value = abs(_scrollVelocity) * 0.1 clamped to [0, 1]

    // time
    record.mesh.material.uniforms.time.value = clock.elapsedTime

    // hover
    record.mesh.material.uniforms.isHovered.value = (record.data.index === _hoveredIndex) ? 1.0 : 0.0

  // 3. Render
  renderer.render(scene, camera)
```

Opacity piecewise lerp helper (module-level pure function, takes n and threshold constants, returns number):
```ts
function computeOpacity(n: number): number {
  if (n < FADE_IN_START)  return 0;
  if (n < FADE_IN_END)    return (n - FADE_IN_START) / (FADE_IN_END - FADE_IN_START);
  if (n < FADE_OUT_START) return 1;
  if (n < FADE_OUT_END)   return 1 - (n - FADE_OUT_START) / (FADE_OUT_END - FADE_OUT_START);
  return 0;
}
```

Similarly `computeBlur(n)` returns 0→MAX_BLUR in `[BLUR_IN_START, BLUR_IN_END]`, MAX_BLUR→0 in `[BLUR_OUT_START, BLUR_OUT_END]`, capped at MAX_BLUR.

